Coordinate declarative day-0 platform bootstrap

Usage:
  bootwright [command]

Examples:
  bootwright help context init
  bootwright version
  bootwright validate --file ./input

Available Commands:
  add-ons                       Manage add-ons
  apply                         Apply the complete selected lifecycle unit
  cluster                       Manage cluster
  completion                    Manage completion
  context                       Manage context
  destroy                       Destroy the complete selected lifecycle unit
  help                          Show human help for an exact command path
  machine                       Manage machine
  media                         Manage media
  plan                          Preview the next complete lifecycle operation
  preflight                     Manage preflight
  render                        Render external-tool artifacts (unavailable)
  secret                        Manage secret
  setup                         Set up context-independent controller prerequisites
  status                        Show context readiness and lifecycle state
  validate                      Validate a complete desired-state input universe
  version                       Show executable and dependency build identities

Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines

Use "bootwright [command] --help" for more information about a command.
